1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,400
On most ships, the 440 V network is an IT system.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:08,900
No phase is connected to the hull.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:14,800
The fan gets an earth fault on L1. Nothing trips. Just an alarm.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,900
But now L2 and L3 sit at 440 V to the hull.

5
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:27,600
A second earth fault, on another phase, is a short circuit.

6
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:33,900
A breaker trips. Maybe on the steering gear.

7
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:39,900
So no. The alarm means: find the fault. Now.
